{"name":"Blue Loneliness","hex":"#486d83","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"loneliness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of depression resulting from being alone or from having no companions.","The condition or state of being alone or having no companions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loneliness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loneliness","blocks":[{"text":"Loneliness is an unpleasant emotional response to perceived or actual social isolation. Loneliness has been described as social pain, a psychological mechanism that motivates individuals to seek social connections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Thoma_Loneliness.jpg/330px-Thoma_Loneliness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loneliness"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Thomas_Wolfe_1937_1_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Thomas_Wolfe_1937_1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Thomas_Wolfe_1937_1_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Thomas_Wolfe_1937_1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Thomas Wolfe who, in an often quoted passage, stated \"The whole conviction of my life now rests upon the belief that loneliness, far from being a rare and curious phenomenon, is the central and inevitable fact of human existence.\"[3] ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThomas_Wolfe_1937_1_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Following_the_Equator_%28Mark_Twain%29_%28page_6_crop%29.jpg/500px-Following_the_Equator_%28Mark_Twain%29_%28page_6_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Following_the_Equator_%28Mark_Twain%29_%28page_6_crop%29.jpg/500px-Following_the_Equator_%28Mark_Twain%29_%28page_6_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Be good & you will be lonesome.\" wrote Mark Twain in Following the Equator (1897)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFollowing_the_Equator_(Mark_Twain)_(page_6_crop).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Nighthawks_by_Edward_Hopper_1942.jpg/500px-Nighthawks_by_Edward_Hopper_1942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum